<title>USA: Owens completes Fibreboard tender.</title>
<headline>Owens completes Fibreboard tender.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens Corning said Friday it completed its $55 per share tender offer for Fibreboard Corp.</p>
<p>The company said shareholders tendered 7.8 million shares, or 92 percent, of Fibreboard as of Thursday. The remaining shares will each convert to $55 in cash, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The glass fiber company said on May 28 it planned to buy Fibreboard for $515 million plus the assumption of $85 million in debt. Fibreboard shares eased 1/16 to 54-3/4 early Friday.</p>
<p>Owens said it expected the merger to be effective early July. Its stock traded at 42-7/8 Friday morning, up 1/16.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
